</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><i>&#160;</i></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><i>Revenue</i></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">Revenues decreased by $36,958,194,
or 34.16%, to $71,241,683 for the year ended September 30, 2025, from $108,199,877 for the year ended September 30, 2024. The decrease
in revenues was primarily driven by the following factors:</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">&#160;</p><div>

</div><table cellpadding="0" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; border-spacing: 0px;">
  <tr>
    <td style="width: 0.5in; padding: 0.75pt 0.75pt 8pt; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</td>
    <td style="white-space: nowrap; vertical-align: top; width: 0.25in; padding-bottom: 10pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 10pt"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">1)</span></td>
    <td style="padding-bottom: 10pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 10pt"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">During the fiscal year 2025, the global economic recovery remained slow, and domestic construction and real estate sectors continued to face weak demand recovery, resulting in weaker overall customer purchase for piping systems compared to fiscal year 2024. While the company maintained its pricing strategy to mitigate persistent cost pressures, the weakness in downstream demand&#8212;coupled with intensified industry competition&#8212;led to a sharp shrink in sales volume, which was the primary driver of the revenue decline.</span></td></tr>
  </table><div>
</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&#160;</p><div>

</div><table cellpadding="0" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; border-spacing: 0px;">
  <tr>
    <td style="width: 0.5in; padding: 0.75pt 0.75pt 8pt">&#160;</td>
    <td style="white-space: nowrap; vertical-align: top; width: 0.25in; padding-bottom: 10pt; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">2)</span></td>
    <td style="padding-bottom: 10pt; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">During the fiscal year 2025, the Company decreased sales of low-margin products, primarily the electrolytic nickel products, from approximately $63.67 million during fiscal year 2024 to approximately $39.76 million during fiscal year 2025. The sales of the electrolytic nickel products accounted to 55.81% of total sales as compared to 58.85% in fiscal year 2024.</span></td></tr>
  </table><div>
</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&#160;</p><div>

</div><table cellpadding="0" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; border-spacing: 0px;">
  <tr>
    <td style="width: 0.5in; padding: 0.75pt 0.75pt 8pt">&#160;</td>
    <td style="white-space: nowrap; vertical-align: top; width: 0.25in; padding-bottom: 8pt; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">3)</span></td>
    <td style="padding-bottom: 8pt; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">In fiscal 2025, raw material price volatility persisted, with nickel (a key input for stainless steel) prices remaining at high levels and other core materials like steel strips experiencing ongoing fluctuations. Despite incremental adjustments to the weighted average selling price (ASP), sustained cost inflation and reduced customer purchasing power amid economic uncertainties further eroded sales performance, contributing to the revenue drop. Due to the increase in product prices, our overall sales volume has declined. For instance, while the sales volume of steel pipes and pipe fittings experienced only slight increase, the sales volume of steel strips grew. However, the overall competitive market environment and external economic factors hindered sales from achieving the expected growth rate, thereby impacting overall revenue performance.</span></td></tr>
  </table><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">Revenues decreased by $3,399,809,
or 3.05%, to $108,199,877 for the year ended September 30, 2024, from $111,599,686 for the year ended September 30, 2023. The decrease
in revenues was primarily driven by the following factors:</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">&#160;</p><div>

</div><table cellpadding="0" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; border-spacing: 0px;">
  <tr>
    <td style="padding: 0.75pt; width: 0.5in">&#160; &#160;</td>
    <td style="white-space: nowrap; vertical-align: top; width: 0.25in; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">1)</span></td>
    <td style="text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">During the fiscal year 2024, we observed a recovery in the real estate market, which led to an increase in market demand. This contrasts with the market pressure faced in fiscal year 2023, particularly due to the downturn in the Chinese real estate market, exacerbated by the collapse of Evergrande. The recovery in 2024 provided us with more favorable sales opportunities. In response to rising raw material costs, the company increased its weighted average selling price (ASP) to sustain profit margins. However, despite the demand recovery, this pricing strategy did not fully offset the negative impact of escalating costs. The price increases led to the loss of price-sensitive customers and heightened market competition, which ultimately resulted in a decline in overall sales and adversely affected revenue.</span></td></tr>
  </table><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&#160;</p><div>

</div><table cellpadding="0" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; border-spacing: 0px;">
  <tr>
    <td style="width: 0.5in; padding-top: 0.75pt; padding-right: 0.75pt; padding-left: 0.75pt">&#160;</td>
    <td style="white-space: nowrap; vertical-align: top; width: 0.25in; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">2)</span></td>
    <td style="text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">During the fiscal year 2024, raw material prices continued to rise, particularly the price of nickel used in stainless steel, which increased production costs. This situation differed from the fluctuations in raw material prices observed in fiscal year 2023. Although nickel prices surged by 33.33% in 2023, the company responded by lowering sales prices to expand market share. However, in fiscal year 2024, while we adjusted our pricing strategy to mitigate the rising costs, the price increases were not sufficient to fully offset the pressure from higher production costs, leading to a decline in revenue.</span></td></tr>
  </table><div>
</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&#160;</p><div>

</div><table cellpadding="0" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; border-spacing: 0px;">
  <tr>
    <td style="width: 0.5in; padding-top: 0.75pt; padding-right: 0.75pt; padding-left: 0.75pt">&#160;</td>
    <td style="white-space: nowrap; vertical-align: top; width: 0.25in; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">3)</span></td>
    <td style="text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Due to the increase in product prices, our overall sales volume has declined. For instance, while the sales volume of steel pipes and pipe fittings experienced only a slight increase, the sales volume of steel strips grew. However, the overall competitive market environment and external economic factors hindered sales from achieving the expected growth rate, thereby impacting overall revenue performance.</span></td></tr>
  </table><div>

</div><p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"><span style="font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p><div>
</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><i>Gross profit</i></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">Our gross profit decreased
by $2,507,004, or 38.29%, to $4,040,192 for the year ended September 30, 2025 from $6,547,196 for the year ended September 30, 2024. Gross
profit margin was 5.67% for the year ended September 30, 2025, as compared to 6.05% for the year ended September 30, 2024. The decrease
in gross profit was primarily driven by a sharp decline in revenue volume, which outpaced the reduction in cost of sales, as well as ongoing
pressure from raw material price volatility that continued to weigh on gross margins despite operational efficiency improvements.</p><div>
</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">Our gross profit increased
by $5,250,780 or 405.023% to $6,547,196 for the year ended September 30, 2024 from $1,296,416 for the year ended September 30, 2023. Gross
profit margin was 6.05% for the year ended September 30, 2024, as compared to 1.16% for the year ended September 30, 2023. The increase
in gross profit was primarily driven by a rise in the weighted average selling price, which offset the pressure from rising costs. Additionally,
the decline in sales costs relative to revenue was more significant, further contributing to the improvement in gross profit.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"></p><div>

</div><!-- Field: Page; Sequence: 52; Value: 1 --><div>
