</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><i>&#160;</i></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><i>Selling and Marketing Expenses</i></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">We incurred $1,531,222 in selling and marketing expenses for the fiscal year ended September 30, 2025, compared to $1,639,873 for the
fiscal year ended September 30, 2024. Selling and marketing expenses decreased by $108,651 or 6.63%, during the fiscal year ended September
30, 2025 compared to the fiscal year ended September 30, 2024. This decrease is primarily due to decreases in sales payroll expenses,
compensation for the sales personnel, freight expenses, and transportation fee during the year.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">We incurred $1,639,873
in selling and marketing expenses for the fiscal year ended September 30, 2024, compared to $2,117,810 for the fiscal year ended
September 30, 2023. Selling and marketing expenses decreased by $477,937 or 22.57%, during the fiscal year ended September 30, 2024
compared to the fiscal year ended September 30, 2023. This decrease is primarily due to decreases in sales payroll expenses,
compensation for the sales personnel, freight expenses, and transportation fee during the year.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><i>&#160;</i></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><i>General and Administrative expenses</i></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">We incurred $4,145,269 in general and administrative expenses for the fiscal year ended September 30, 2025, compared to $4,829,103 for
the fiscal year ended September 30, 2024. General and administrative expenses decreased by $683,834, or 14.16%, for the fiscal year ended
September 30, 2025 compared to the fiscal year ended September 30, 2024. The decrease is mainly attributable to the decreased employee
compensation and benefit expense incurred during the fiscal year 2025.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">We incurred $4,829,103 in
general and administrative expenses for the fiscal year ended September 30, 2024, compared to $5,144,340 for the fiscal year ended September
30, 2023. General and administrative expenses decreased by $315,237, or 6.13%, for the fiscal year ended September 30, 2024 compared to
the fiscal year ended September 30, 2023. The decrease is mainly attributable to the decreased employee compensation and benefit expense
incurred during the fiscal year 2024.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in"><i>&#160;</i></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><i>Asset impairment costs</i></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">We incurred $1,757,042 in asset impairment costs for the fiscal year ended September 30, 2025, compared to $599,709 for the fiscal year
ended September 30, 2024. Asset impairment costs increased by $1,157,333 or 192.98%, during the fiscal year ended September 30, 2025 compared
to the fiscal year ended September 30, 2024. This increase is primarily due to the bad debt allowances recognized for long-aged accounts
receivable during 2025 fiscal year.</p><div>

